# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party asset packs. These are commercial or otherwise non-redistributable
# and must be acquired separately -- see docs/SETUP.md. Never commit them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/[Aa]ssets/(HDRP)*
/[Aa]ssets/GrassFlowers
/[Aa]ssets/Realistic Tree
/[Aa]ssets/RP_Character
/[Aa]ssets/TerrainSampleAssets

# Textures derived from Renderpeople scans. Derivative works of a commercial
# licence -- regenerate locally, never commit. See docs/SETUP.md.
/[Aa]ssets/Materials/Modified_Textures/rp_*.png
/[Aa]ssets/Materials/Modified_Textures/rp_*.png.meta

# Flattened HSR prefab produced by re-importing the URDF. Not referenced by the
# study scene, which uses the per-link prefabs under
# Assets/Models/hsr_description_v2/robots/ -- those ARE tracked, because the
# scene addresses them by GUID and regenerating would not reproduce those GUIDs.
/[Aa]ssets/HSR/
/[Aa]ssets/HSR.meta

# HDRP global settings, auto-generated on first open. The originals ship inside
# the NYC buildings asset pack, which is not redistributable (above), so Unity
# recreates them in any clone that lacks the pack. Harmless and machine-local;
# ProjectSettings/GraphicsSettings.asset keeps pointing at the pack's copy so
# that installing the pack per docs/SETUP.md resolves cleanly.
/[Aa]ssets/HDRPDefaultResources/
/[Aa]ssets/HDRPDefaultResources.meta

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Human-subject data. Only the de-identified release under data/ is tracked.
# Raw exports and per-participant run output stay local.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/analysis/raw_data/
/analysis/participant_configs/
/analysis/launch_scripts/
/analysis/results/
/analysis/end_question_plots/
/analysis/output/
/analysis/**/*.html

# The released dataset under data/ IS tracked. It is generated by
# analysis/deidentify.py from raw exports that must never be committed
# (analysis/raw_data/, ignored above). See docs/ETHICS.md.

